course: dictionary
lesson: 12956
title: Saying it with feeling
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Writers want you to hear how a character speaks, not just what they say. Instead of writing «said» again and again, they can choose a word that shows the feeling. To exclaim means to say something suddenly and loudly, because you feel surprise, joy, anger or pain.
explain: «"We won!" exclaimed Maya, jumping up from her seat.» The exclamation mark and the word jumping tell you Maya is thrilled. She is not just speaking; she is shouting out with joy. Exclaimed shows that feeling in one word.
explain: Exclaim is not the same as say. You can say something quietly and calmly, but you exclaim something loudly and suddenly. Try your meaning in the sentence: if the character is calm and quiet, exclaim will not fit.
explain: Use exclaim with direct speech, the words a speaker says inside speech marks, like «"Look out!" he exclaimed.» Teachers often suggest exclaim instead of said to make your writing more lively.
fact: Exclaim means to say or shout something suddenly and loudly.
fact: People exclaim because they feel surprise, joy, anger or pain.
fact: The forms are exclaim, exclaims, exclaimed and exclaiming.
fact: «"Look!" she exclaimed.» shows that she is excited or surprised.
fact: Writers use exclaim instead of said to show how a character feels.
exercise: «"The sea is freezing!" Sam exclaimed as he jumped in.» What does exclaimed mean here? | Asked a question politely | Ate slowly while sitting down | *Said suddenly and loudly, because of surprise or shock | Whispered quietly to himself
exercise: «"A rainbow!" Ella ____.» Choose the best word to fill the gap. | whispered | sighed | yawned | *exclaimed
exercise: Nadia says exclaim means the same as whisper. Is she right? | No, exclaim means to say something loudly and suddenly | Yes, exclaim means to say something quietly | *No, exclaim means to say something loudly and suddenly, so it is the opposite of whisper | Yes, because both are ways of speaking
test: «"Stop!" the teacher exclaimed, as the ball flew towards the window.» Why would a writer choose exclaimed here? | To show the teacher was whispering a secret | To show the teacher was bored and sleepy | To show the teacher was asking a question | *To show the teacher was suddenly alarmed and shouting
test: «"I passed my test!" Priya ____.» Which word best shows her excitement? | *exclaimed | sighed | mumbled | yawned
exam: «"Happy birthday!" everyone ____ together.» Choose the correct form of exclaim. | *exclaimed | exclaim | exclaims | exclaiming
